<title>USA: Exxon in talks for more Soviet reserves.</title>
<headline>Exxon in talks for more Soviet reserves.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp is in exclusive negotiations which would add 10 billion barrels to reserves of oil equivalent in the former Soviet Union, chief executive Lee Raymond told the Howard Weil Energy Conference Monday.</p>
<p>He noted the company already has rights to 10 billion barrels of reserves in the former Soviet Union.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
